"## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design fault-tolerant Unix log ingestion across mixed formats, archives, and rotation, with checkpointing and deduplication.

## Key Concepts

- Log rotation and gz archives
- Mixed log formats (text and JSON)
- Multi-line event parsing
- Event deduplication using fingerprints
- Persistent state and restart safety

## Code Example

```javascript
// Fingerprint function for deduplication
function fingerprint(hour, message) {
  const normalized = (message || '').toLowerCase().trim();
  const hash = require('crypto').createHash('sha256');
  hash.update(`${hour}:${normalized}`);
  return hash.digest('hex');
}

// Checkpoint persistence
function saveCheckpoint(checkpoint) {
  const tempPath = '/tmp/checkpoint.json';
  fs.writeFileSync(tempPath, JSON.stringify(checkpoint));
  fs.renameSync(tempPath, '/path/to/checkpoints.json');
}
```"

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to handle mixed text and JSON logs, manage log rotation and compression, and perform cross-host aggregation with time-based filtering. It tests regex parsing, time-windowing, deduplication logic, and working within POSIX shell constraints without external dependencies.

## Key Concepts
- POSIX shell constraints with gzipped logs and mixed formats
- Time-window filtering for the last 30 minutes
- Robust user extraction from both plaintext and JSON logs
- Case-insensitive deduplication with per-host aggregation

## Code Example
```bash
for host in $(awk -F'[/=]' '/^\/(logs|var)\/log\// && !/^#/ {print $3}' /etc/hosts 2>/dev/null | sort -u); do
  users=$(find "/logs" -name '*.log*' -mmin -30 2>/dev/null | \
    xargs -I{} sh -c 'zcat -f "{}" 2>/dev/null' | \
    awk -v host="$host" '
      BEGIN {now=systime(); cutoff=now-1800}
      /^[[:space:]]/ {next}
      /^"?[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}/ {
        gsub(/[\[\]:]/, "", $1" "$2)
        cmd="date -d \""$1" "$2"\" +%s 2>/dev/null || date -d 0 +%s"
        cmd | getline ts; close(cmd)
        if (ts >= cutoff) {
          if ($0 ~ /ERROR|WARN/) {
            for (i=1; i<=NF; i++) {
              if ($i ~ /^user[=:]/) {
                gsub(/[,:"\047]/, "", $(i+1))
                print tolower($(i+1))
              }
            }
          }
        }
        next
      }
      /^"?\{/ {
        if (match($0, /"ts"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*"([^"]+)"/, t)) {
          cmd="date -d \""t[1]"\" +%s 2>/dev/null || date -d 0 +%s"
          cmd | getline ts; close(cmd)
          if (ts >= cutoff && match($0, /"user"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*"([^"]+)"/, u)) {
            print tolower(u[1])
          }
        }
        next
      }
    ' | sort -u | wc -l)
  echo "$host: $users unique users"
done
```
